  "text": "Classic Neapolitan ice cream is a delightful combination of three flavors: vanilla, chocolate, and strawberry. Here's a simple recipe to make your own at home, using basic ingredients you can find in most kitchens:\n\n### **Classic Neapolitan Ice Cream Recipe**\n\n#### **Ingredients** (Makes about 4\u20136 servings)\n\n**Vanilla Ice Cream:**\n- 2 cups whole milk\n- 1 cup heavy cream\n- 3/4 cup sugar\n- 1 vanilla bean (or 1 teaspoon vanilla extract)\n- 1/2 tsp salt\n\n**Chocolate Ice Cream:**\n- 2 cups whole milk\n- 1 cup heavy cream\n- 3/4 cup sugar\n- 1/4 cup cocoa powder\n- 1/2 tsp salt\n- 1/2 tsp vanilla extract\n\n**Strawberry Ice Cream:**\n- 2 cups whole milk\n- 1 cup heavy cream\n- 3/4 cup sugar\n- 1/2 cup fresh strawberries, mashed\n- 1/2 tsp vanilla extract\n\n#### **Instructions**\n\n1. **Make the Vanilla Ice Cream:**\n   - In a saucepan, combine the milk, cream, sugar, vanilla bean (split and scraped), and salt. Heat over medium heat until the sugar dissolves, stirring constantly.\n   - Pour the mixture into a bowl and let it cool to room temperature.\n   - Churn in an ice cream maker according to the manufacturer's instructions until it reaches a soft-serve consistency.\n   - Freeze until firm.\n\n2. **Make the Chocolate Ice Cream:**\n   - In a saucepan, combine the milk, cream, sugar, cocoa powder, salt, and vanilla extract. Heat over medium heat until the sugar dissolves.\n   - Cool to room temperature, then churn in an ice cream maker as directed.\n   - Freeze until firm.\n\n3. **Make the Strawberry Ice Cream:**\n   - In a saucepan, combine the milk, cream, sugar, mashed strawberries, and vanilla extract. Heat over medium heat until the sugar dissolves and the mixture is warm.\n   - Cool to room temperature, then churn in an ice cream maker.\n   - Freeze until firm.\n\n4. **Assemble the Neapolitan Ice Cream:**\n   - Scoop the three flavors into a container, layering them one at a time (vanilla, chocolate, strawberry or any order you prefer).\n   - Freeze until fully set, at least 4 hours or overnight.\n\n5. **Serve:**\n   - Let the ice cream sit for a few minutes to soften slightly before serving.\n\n**Tip:** If you don\u2019t have an ice cream maker, you can make \"no-churn\" versions of these ice creams using whipped cream and frozen custard base for a quicker version.\n\nEnjoy your homemade Neapolitan ice cream!",
